   "notes": "Henry Martyn Hall, 24 Market Street (1887, Gothic): cobble/flint walling with ashlar bands and dressings, front gable to Market Street (apex above eave). x from p0 at the east (churchyard) corner. Canted stone oriel over the east corner carrying 3-light traceried windows through the upper hall level; ground: chequer-tympanum pointed arch window, large pointed shop arch ('size?'), smaller chequer arch window at west; sloping stone weathering/hood over the ground floor; tall 2-light traceried hall window in the gable centre; small square window near the west edge."
